WEBVTT

00:12:58.621 --> 00:13:00.746
Some, as had I, would remember.

00:13:01.829 --> 00:13:04.287
The report finished and Abed spoke.

00:13:05.162 --> 00:13:06.704
"It is a pity," he said,

00:13:06.746 --> 00:13:10.162
"that the police in this country
are not tough enough on bad drivers."

00:13:10.496 --> 00:13:12.329
(Laughter)

00:13:12.371 --> 00:13:13.996
I was baffled.

00:13:15.329 --> 00:13:17.454
Abed had said something remarkable.

00:13:18.162 --> 00:13:19.454
Did it point up the degree

00:13:19.496 --> 00:13:21.746
to which he'd absolved
himself of the crash?

00:13:21.746 --> 00:13:23.579
Was it evidence of guilt, an assertion

00:13:23.621 --> 00:13:25.829
that he should have been put away longer?

00:13:25.829 --> 00:13:29.621
He'd served six months in prison,
lost his truck license for a decade.

00:13:29.662 --> 00:13:31.579
I forgot my discretion.